WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.499 --> 00:00:12.740
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and quite possibly
the greatest episode of sherlock just aired.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.599
Since a lot of you might not have seen it
yet I’ll try to keep out as many spoilers

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:16.599
as possible, but be careful.

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:18.190
I’m also taking questions in the comments
for this video for my sign of three q and

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.190
a video tomorrow.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.570
so if you have a question about episode 2
and want me to include it in the video.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.430
Be sure to write it in the comments below.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.930
I’ll post my breakdown a couple days after
that.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:29.949
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:32.899
So just like my last review I’m going to
do my Top 5 favorite things from the episode

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.040
and then my overall review.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:37.010
So let’s go, we gotta keep this stag party
on schedule.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.300
Number 5 - The editing.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.780
Normally I talk about parts of the story,
but there was this incredible way the story

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.750
was told in several different scenes even
when sherlock wasn’t in his mind palace.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.520
I love how sherlock essentially shows you
the end result first and then rewinds to show

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.610
you how they got there.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:58.280
Like learning how sherlock became watson’s
best man while he was in the middle of his

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.280
wedding speech.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.890
They’ve done mechanical things like this
with the story for a long time, but something

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:07.020
about this episode and the bright colors of
the wedding juxtaposed with the drab colors

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.760
of baker street just made it feel like you
were jumping down the rabbit hole of sherlock’s

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.760
past.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.580
And the whole time the joke is on sherlock.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:19.310
The series makes fun of him a lot, but this
episode was sherlock walking right into a

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:22.100
face full of pie.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:27.340
4 - Sherlock Stag Party - Watching the writers
explain to us what sherlock and watson would

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.000
do at a stag party was amazing.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.240
It’s a fair question, what would those two
do?

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.720
The general decline of the evening into what
ended as the funniest cases they’ve ever

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.370
attempted was brilliant.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.259
I’m totally inviting drunk sherlock to my
stag party.

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:43.909
And we’re going to solve the shit out of
some cases.

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:45.890
3 - Sherlock’s Wedding Speech.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:52.580
It’s a wedding episode and of course sherlock
was always going to be the best man.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:58.310
But first watching a side character get her
own montage was so much fun and two, the comedy

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.360
of sherlock’s actual speech was so much
funnier when it got tied up in the greater

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.229
murder mystery.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:08.910
It was like having a conversation with someone
who was flipping channels on the television.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:13.599
Constantly jumping around in time and space,
or time and headspace.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:17.200
2 - The Mind Palace internet chat room.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.540
So let’s try not to spoil this too much
for people who haven’t seen it yet, because

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.220
a very notable character appears inside the
mind palace.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:28.070
But just from a production stand point, seeing
the camera jump back and forth between the

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:32.780
real world and this really big set that looked
like an orchestra pit was so clever.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.040
It was almost like sherlock was conducting
a symphony in his mind while carrying on a

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.090
conversation with all the chat room women.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:45.280
I was also really impressed at how they visualized
sherlock imagining each woman changing as

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.790
a result of answers they gave him.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:55.360
Of all the scenes I would think that that
would have taken the longest to shoot.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.700
1- Soul Man Sherlock.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.200
So without going into the plot or the more
specific details, a lot of people’s complaints

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.730
about Sherlock in episode 1 being a dick are
answered in this episode.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:08.730
Throughout sherlock demonstrates that he’s
much more complex than we thought.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.260
We actually learn a couple new things about
his personality and they place him in this

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.769
much warmer context.

00:03:14.769 --> 00:03:20.400
If mycroft is the barometer for coldness,
then sherlock just became so much more precious

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:28.100
to 
the fandom.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.130
Overall this was my favorite episode of the
series so far.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:34.104
Just to give you an idea for how I feel this
series fits into context with series 1 and

00:03:34.104 --> 00:03:35.104
2, before sign of three.

00:03:35.104 --> 00:03:36.104
My favorite episode was empty hearse.

00:03:36.104 --> 00:03:37.549
So far each new episode this year has been
my new favorite.

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:43.800
I don’t think his last vow will be able
to top the preciousness of this episode, just

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:50.049
because weddings are so ripe for comedy and
character relationships.

00:03:50.049 --> 00:03:54.300
As i mentioned earlier, the way the story
was told was so much more fun jumping around

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.030
in time and space so much.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:59.189
Mostly because the filming locations looked
so different.

00:03:59.189 --> 00:04:13.690
And even though they could have just decided
to have fun with watson’s stag party or

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:18.620
sherlock at the wedding, each moment was really
true to the characters and the larger story

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.870
of the murder mystery.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:23.120
The episode also gave me some practical help.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.740
I just found out which game I’m going to
play at my next party.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.230
Try and guess what I’m talking about in
the comments.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:33.430
and Let me know what your favorite moment
was.

